        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. 'Nothing like COVID': Expert urges calm over hantavirus outbreak on cruise ship Europe Issued on: 10/05/2026 - 15:00 Modified: 10/05/2026 - 15:17 Medical experts say the hantavirus outbreak linked to a cruise ship remains contained and should not trigger fears of another Covid-style crisis. Speaking to FRANCE 24, former Institut Pasteur chief Christian Bréchot said human-to-human transmission of the virus is rare, but warned the incident highlights the need for faster testing and stronger outbreak response systems worldwide. Scottish independence calls grow after Labour losses shake Starmer’s leadership 10/05/2026 Europe Hantavirus poses 'very little risk' to wider public, health expert says 10/05/2026 Europe International evacuation underway as cruise ship passengers return home 10/05/2026 Europe Starmer vows to stay on after local elections deliver losses for Labour 10/05/2026 Europe Hantavirus-hit cruise ship arrives at Tenerife in Spain's Canary Islands 10/05/2026 Europe Ukrainians mark end of WWII amid fragile ceasefire with Russia 09/05/2026 Europe Contact tracing begins after Hantavirus-hit cruise passengers disembarks in St. Helena 09/05/2026 Europe Moscow marks Victory Day amid tight security 09/05/2026 Europe 'Atmosphere closer to wartime': Moscow’s muted Victory Day reflects growing security fears 09/05/2026 Europe"
